      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>The element source can be modified concurrently by multiple threads without external synchronization. The spliterator should document the effect of modifications during traversal. A top-level spliterator should not report both <c>Concurrent</c> and <see cref="F:Java.Util.SpliteratorCharacteristics.Sized" />, because its size can change during traversal. A sub-spliterator can report <c>Sized</c> if its size is known and traversal does not reflect additions or removals. A top-level spliterator should not report both <c>Concurrent</c> and <see cref="F:Java.Util.SpliteratorCharacteristics.Immutable" />, because they are mutually exclusive. A sub-spliterator can report <c>Immutable</c> if traversal does not reflect additions or removals. A top-level spliterator with either inconsistent combination provides no guarantees for computations that use it.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/util/Spliterator.html#CONCURRENT" title="Reference documentation">Java reference for <code>java.util.Spliterator.CONCURRENT</code>.</a></format></para>
        </summary>
        <remarks>
          <para>Portions of this page are modifications based on work created and shared by the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/site-policies" title="Android Open Source Project">Android Open Source Project</a></format> and used according to terms described in the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5/" title="Creative Commons 2.5 Attribution License">Creative Commons 2.5 Attribution License.</a></format></para>
        </remarks>
      </Docs>
    </Member>
