      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>The element source cannot be structurally modified: elements cannot be added, replaced, or removed during traversal. A spliterator that reports neither <c>Immutable</c> nor <see cref="F:Java.Util.SpliteratorCharacteristics.Concurrent" /> should document its policy for structural interference detected during traversal, such as throwing <see cref="T:Java.Util.ConcurrentModificationException" />.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/util/Spliterator.html#IMMUTABLE" title="Reference documentation">Java reference for <code>java.util.Spliterator.IMMUTABLE</code>.</a></format></para>
        </summary>
        <remarks>
