      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>An encounter order is defined for the elements. <see cref="M:Java.Util.ISpliterator.TrySplit" /> splits a strict prefix, <see cref="M:Java.Util.ISpliterator.TryAdvance(Java.Util.Functions.IConsumer)" /> advances one element in prefix order, and <see cref="M:Java.Util.ISpliterator.ForEachRemaining(Java.Util.Functions.IConsumer)" /> performs actions in encounter order. A collection has an encounter order if its <see cref="M:Java.Util.ICollection.Iterator" /> method documents an order; the encounter order is the same as that order. Otherwise, the collection has no encounter order.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/util/Spliterator.html#ORDERED" title="Reference documentation">Java reference for <code>java.util.Spliterator.ORDERED</code>.</a></format></para>
